All done. Here's what was added:

**`txtar/archive.go`** — `Lookup` method (documented in the same style as `Format`, `Parse`, etc.):
```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false
// when the archive has no such file.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	for i := range a.Files {
		if a.Files[i].Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — `TestArchiveLookup` covering both outcomes:
- **Found**: looks up `"foo"` and verifies the returned `*File` has the correct name and data.
- **Not found**: looks up `"baz"` and verifies it returns `(nil, false)`.

All tests pass (`ok golang.org/x/tools/txtar`).

